<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  iCloud RELEASE variant of the Mac entitlements (i2). This is a SUPERSET of
  WhisperClipboard.entitlements: it adds CloudKit for cross-device history sync.

  WHY A SEPARATE FILE:
    The default project (WhisperClipboard.entitlements) stays minimal so the
    ad-hoc-signed dev / CI verify build launches with no provisioning profile.
    Adding iCloud entitlements to an ad-hoc build can BLOCK launch (the OS
    validates the container against a profile that ad-hoc signing can't carry).
    So this variant is used ONLY by the Developer-ID release signing step, which
    also embeds a matching provisioning profile.

  HOW TO USE (release only — see Packaging/RELEASING.md):
    Sign with:  --entitlements WhisperClipboard/WhisperClipboard-iCloud.entitlements
    AND embed a Developer-ID provisioning profile that includes the
    iCloud.nl.nielscroiset.whisperclipboard container.
    Runtime dormancy (HistorySyncEngine.accountIsAvailable) means an ad-hoc build
    that never gets this entitlement simply shows "iCloud niet beschikbaar" — it
    does not crash — so day-to-day dev is unaffected.

  TODO(Niels) — developer portal, one-time (NOT automatable here):
    1. Apple Developer portal → Identifiers → App IDs: ensure the Mac App ID
       nl.nielscroiset.whisperclipboard has the iCloud capability enabled and is
       associated with the CloudKit container
       iCloud.nl.nielscroiset.whisperclipboard (create the container if absent).
    2. Do the same for the iOS App ID nl.nielscroiset.whisperclipboard.ios,
       pointing at the SAME container so both platforms share one private zone.
    3. Create a Developer-ID provisioning profile for the Mac App ID that
       includes the iCloud container, download it, and reference it in the
       release signing step (build_release.sh).
    4. In CloudKit Console, deploy the "Transcript" record type schema to
       Production before shipping (dev schema is auto-created on first write).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudKit</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.nl.nielscroiset.whisperclipboard</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
